      en: "Ebey Island Battery is a historic World War II coastal battery on Kwajalein Atoll. It was built by the Japanese to defend the entrance to Kwajalein Atoll. The battery consists of several gun positions and bunkers. During the Battle of Kwajalein in February 1944, US forces attacked the battery and captured it after heavy fighting. The remains of the battery are still visible today and are a popular destination for historical walking tours. The facility is a testament to the intense warfare in the Pacific. Local tours offer insights into Japanese military tactics. Ebey Island Battery recalls the strategic importance of the Marshall Islands during the war.",
