      en: "The Majuro WWII Memorial is a commemorative site on Majuro Atoll that honors the victims of World War II in the Marshall Islands. It was erected in 1994 on the 50th anniversary of the Battle of Kwajalein. The memorial consists of a stone plaque listing the names of the fallen and a small park. It is located near the government building in Delap. The memorial honors both Allied and Japanese soldiers. An annual ceremony is held on February 1. The memorial is a place of reflection and a call for peace. It also remembers civilian casualties and the destruction of infrastructure. The site is maintained by local government and veteran organizations.",
